  "reason": "With no completed experiments, the main uncertainty is whether a core multimodal multiprofile pipeline is competitive. config_013 tests a central, moderately strong hypothesis: scGPT RNA representations plus ResNet-50 image features, multiprofile avgpool aggregation, and simple concat fusion. This avoids the highest-cost choices (ViT-L and transformer aggregation) while still probing the likely best modality combination and a strong RNA encoder. It gives an anchor for deciding whether to escalate to stronger image/aggregation/fusion settings or pivot to cheaper encoders. Expected relative cost: medium-low among multimodal multiprofile options, more expensive than unimodal, singleprofile, or PCA-based configs, but cheaper than ViT-L or transformer-aggregation configs."
}

